\[
\int_{-2}^{4} g(x) \, dx = \int_{-2}^{4} (f(x) + 3) \, dx = \int_{-2}^{4} f(x) \, dx + \int_{-2}^{4} 3 \, dx
\]

The integral of \( f(x) \) over \([-2, 4]\) is the sum of the areas of the shaded regions A and B, which are given as \( a \) and \( b \) respectively. Since region A is below the x-axis, its area is negative, so:

