The derivative of \( y = \log_2(x) \) is given by:
\[ y' = \frac{d}{dx} \log_2(x) = \frac{1}{x \ln(2)} \]

This derivative tells us that the slope of the tangent line to the curve \( y = \log_2(x) \) at any point \( x \) is inversely proportional to \( x \). As \( x \) increases, the slope of the tangent line decreases.

