The integral in question is:
\[
\int_1^{\infty} \frac{1}{x^{0.99}} \, dx
\]

This is an improper integral, and we can evaluate it by considering the limit:
\[
\lim_{b \to \infty} \int_1^b \frac{1}{x^{0.99}} \, dx
\]

First, we find the antiderivative of \(\frac{1}{x^{0.99}}\):
\[
\int \frac{1}{x^{0.99}} \, dx = \int x^{-0.99} \, dx = \frac{x^{0.01}}{0.01} + C = 100x^{0.01} + C
\]

