   - The hexagon can be divided into 6 equilateral triangles, each with side length 1.
   - The area of one equilateral triangle with side length 1 is:
     \[
     \text{Area of one triangle} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \times 1^2 = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}
     \]
