 To solve this problem, we need to understand the mechanical advantage provided by the pulley system. The system consists of three pulleys, which means the mechanical advantage is 3. This means that the distance moved by the load (point Q) is one-third of the distance moved by the effort (point P).

Given:
- Point P is pulled down by 24 cm.

Since the mechanical advantage is 3, the distance moved by point Q upwards will be:

\[
\text{Distance moved by Q} = \frac{\text{Distance moved by P}}{\text{Mechanical Advantage}} = \frac{24 \text{ cm}}{3} = 8 \text{ cm}
\]

Answer: \boxed{8}
