Since the figure is a square and the diameter of the circle is equal to the side length of the square, each side of the square is \(10 \mathrm{~cm}\).

The perimeter \(P\) of a square is given by:
\[
P = 4 \times \text{side length}
\]

Substituting the side length:
\[
P = 4 \times 10 \mathrm{~cm} = 40 \mathrm{~cm}
\]

