\[
\text{Number of cubes} = a + b + c - \gcd(a, b) - \gcd(b, c) - \gcd(c, a) + \gcd(a, b, c)
\]

where \( a \), \( b \), and \( c \) are the dimensions of the cuboid, and \( \gcd \) denotes the greatest common divisor.

